---
/**
 * @category Pages
 * @page-template blog-post
 * @name BlogPost
 *
 * System page template — the canonical wrapper for every rendered blog-post
 * route. Edits to this file propagate to all routes via the existing
 * component-instance system (same mechanism that propagates Header edits).
 *
 * Phase 1: <slot> with FALLBACK sample-post content (2026-08-13). The
 * fallback is what the master editor shows so the template can be styled
 * against realistic content — every element inside it is selectable and
 * class edits persist to this file via the normal write-back path. At
 * runtime the generated post route ALWAYS fills the slot
 * (template-generator.ts renders <BlogPost>…markup…</BlogPost>), so the
 * fallback never ships to a real page or export. Users can add/remove any
 * element AROUND the slot.
 *
 * Fallback constraints (canvasHtml regex pipeline + write-back key parity):
 *   - no nested <slot>, no <script>/<meta>/<title>/<link>/<base>
 *   - no paired Capitalized component tags (self-closing only)
 *   - avoid tags GlobalNav uses (a/div/header/nav/svg/details/summary/path)
 *     so tagname-N keys can't drift on the inlined-nav push path
 *
 * Phase 2 (annotated, not built): replace the slot with a typed binding to
 * collection data via an `@content-source: blog-post` marker and a `post`
 * prop. Do not change the slot ELEMENT itself until Phase 2 ships.
 *   See docs/archive/plans/2026-05-11-pages-in-assets-design.md §"Phase 2".
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from './Header.astro';
import Footer from './Footer.astro';

const { title } = Astro.props;
import GlobalNav from './navigation/GlobalNav.astro';
import Logos from './Logos.astro';
---
<Layout title={title}>
  <GlobalNav />
  <slot>
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600">Engineering</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900">How we cut our build times in half</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-500">A practical walkthrough of the caching, profiling, and one surprising config flag that got our CI from 22 minutes down to 9.</p>
      <section class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <img src="/assets/userpics/userpic03.webp" alt="Author avatar" class="h-10 w-10 rounded-full object-cover" />
        <span class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Alex Rivera</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-gray-400">·</span>
        <time class="text-sm text-gray-500">Aug 13, 2026</time>
      </section>
      <figure class="mt-10">
        <img src="/assets/images/content/hero-bg.webp" alt="Build pipeline dashboard" class="w-full rounded-xl object-cover" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-sm text-gray-400">The pipeline dashboard after the migration.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="mt-10 text-base leading-7 text-gray-700">Every team says their build is slow. Ours actually was: twenty-two minutes from push to green, long enough that people batched commits and reviews queued up overnight. This post is the exact sequence of changes that fixed it, with the numbers for each step.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Start by measuring, not guessing</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-gray-700">We spent the first day only profiling. The breakdown surprised us: dependency install was 40% of the wall clock, tests were 25%, and the bundler — the thing everyone blamed — was under 15%.</p>
      <blockquote class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-blue-600 pl-4 text-lg italic text-gray-600">The slowest part of your build is almost never the part your team complains about.</blockquote>
      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">The three changes that mattered</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-base leading-7 text-gray-700">
        <li>Restored the dependency cache between runs — 8 minutes saved.</li>
        <li>Split the test suite across four shards — 3 minutes saved.</li>
        <li>Turned off source maps on CI builds — 2 minutes saved.</li>
      </ul>
      <figure class="mt-10">
        <img src="/assets/images/content/components.webp" alt="Test shard timing chart" class="w-full rounded-xl object-cover" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-sm text-gray-400">Shard timings after the split — near-even at last.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="mt-10 text-base leading-7 text-gray-700">Nine minutes isn't the floor — but it's fast enough that nobody batches commits anymore, and that changed how the team ships more than any tool could. <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Measure first; the wins are rarely where you think.</strong></p>
    </article>
  </slot>
</Layout>
